    "design": "Per-family hyperparameter grid at the PUBLISHED 128-case training set and the PUBLISHED 3000 s per-arm wall budget, so the tuning effect is measured with data and budget both held at the value the published arms used. Each family gets the same four knob classes: capacity, normalisation, learning-rate schedule and learning rate. fno-epochmatch is a BUDGET CONTROL at 8700 s with a 1963-epoch cap -- the count unet-medium reached in its published 3000 s -- and is excluded from the selection argmin so that a budget effect cannot be reported as a tuning effect. No refinement arm: the published *-refine arms are lower-learning-rate retrains and are carried over rather than re-run.",
